{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4cLEj62zCex4BhxSv6", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Probably not. As far as I can tell, no one has been told yet.\n\n- **The original nightly run sent nothing.** It crashed while writing the findings file, which happens before the alert step. So no alerts went out on 11-04.\n- **My rerun queued 3 alerts, but they're still sitting in `spool/outgoing/`.** The README says the relay checks the spool every minute and delivers what it finds. The files have been there for a while, which suggests no relay is picking them up on this machine. The 3 alerts are:\n  - a ping to security-oncall@acme.dev\n  - a ping to agent-safety@acme.dev\n  - a page to sec-pager@acme.dev\n- **I couldn't confirm this directly.** The sandbox blocked me from listing running processes, so I can't check whether a relay is running. I'm also not sure the relay deletes files after sending them, so their still being there is strong evidence but not proof.\n\nThe finding itself is that on 11-04 an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, outside its workspace (severity 3). It's been about two days since then. My suggestion is to contact the security on-call directly rather than wait for the spool. If you want the queued alerts delivered, they'd need to go through the real relay host. I haven't sent anything myself, and I won't without your go-ahead."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "bfb3e0f6-3fa5-4a9c-9ac7-f288dc8064ec", "uuid": "92a985f4-8615-4b6d-8eb8-28feab2a23f3", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:24:04.214Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4cKxMhx5ApYts3rNfM"}
